<title>USA: Netrix to cut workforce 20 pct.</title>
<headline>Netrix to cut workforce 20 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HERNDON, Va. 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>NETRIX Corp  on Wednesday said it was cutting its workforce by some 20 percent and narrowing its focus as part of a drive to reduce expenses.</p>
<p>The company, a maker of switching products for communications networking, said in a statement the staff cuts would begin to be reflected in its second-quarter results. Lynn Chapman, who was named president and chief executive in January, announced the initiative as the company reported a decline in first-quarter revenues to $8.4 million from $11.2 million in the year-ago period. The company said the drop reflected slower sales of new products.</p>
</text>
